From $a + 2b = 1$, we have $a = 1 - 2b$.  Then
\begin{align*} \frac{2}{a} + \frac{1}{b} &= \frac{2}{1 - 2b} + \frac{1}{b} \\ &= \frac{2}{1 - 2b} + \frac{1}{b} \\ &= \frac{2b + 1 - 2b}{b(1 - 2b)} \\ &= \frac{1}{b(1 - 2b)} \end{align*}
Let $g(b) = \frac{1}{b(1 - 2b)}$.  We want to minimize $g(b)$ for $b > 0$ and $1 - 2b > 0$, so $2b < 1$, i.e., $b < \frac{1}{2}$.
We take the derivative of $g(b)$ with respect to $b$:
\[g'(b) = -\frac{b(1 - 2b) - 1(1 - 4b)}{(b(1 - 2b))^2} = -\frac{b - 2b^2 - 1 + 4b}{(b(1 - 2b))^2} = -\frac{-2b^2 + 5b - 1}{(b(1 - 2b))^2} = \frac{2b^2 - 5b + 1}{(b(1 - 2b))^2}.\]
We want to find where $g'(b) = 0$, which means $2b^2 - 5b + 1 = 0$.  Then
\[b = \frac{5 \pm \sqrt{25 - 8}}{4} = \frac{5 \pm \sqrt{17}}{4}.\]
Since $0 < b < \frac{1}{2}$, we take $b = \frac{5 - \sqrt{17}}{4} \approx \frac{5 - 4.123}{4} \approx \frac{0.877}{4} \approx 0.219$.
When $b = \frac{5 - \sqrt{17}}{4}$, $a = 1 - 2b = 1 - 2 \cdot \frac{5 - \sqrt{17}}{4} = 1 - \frac{5 - \sqrt{17}}{2} = \frac{2 - 5 + \sqrt{17}}{2} = \frac{\sqrt{17} - 3}{2}$.

Then
